# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MarkForge — environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values:
#     cp .env.example .env        (Windows: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit real secrets.
# For the deployed web app, set the SAME variables in Vercel:
#     Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Access gate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The 6-digit PIN users type on the login screen. Exactly 6 digits, numeric.
# Empty falls back to the default 123098. The PIN is also the "sign out
# everywhere" key: rotating it invalidates every session.
APP_PIN=123098

# Signs the session cookie. OPTIONAL but recommended.
# Generate one with:
#     Node      : node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#     PowerShell: [Convert]::ToBase64String((1..32 | ForEach-Object { Get-Random -Maximum 256 }))
# If left empty the app derives a signing key from APP_PIN instead;
# that works, but a dedicated secret lets you rotate them independently.
SESSION_SECRET=

# ── Cloudflare R2 (document storage) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Where every note, image and index lives. Without these four, a local run
# falls back to your disk (fine) and a Vercel deployment loses data between
# requests (not fine).

# 1. Create a bucket: Cloudflare Dashboard → R2 Object Storage → Create bucket.
#    The name you chose goes in R2_BUCKET below.
R2_BUCKET=

# 2. Your Cloudflare Account ID: shown on the R2 overview page
#    (right sidebar, "Account ID") — or under Workers & Pages → Overview.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=

# 3. Create an API token: R2 → Manage R2 API Tokens → Create API token.
#    Choose the "Object Read & Write" permission and scope it to your bucket.
#    The create screen shows both values exactly once — copy them now.
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# ── Optional overrides (sane defaults apply) ─────────────────────────────────

# Key prefixes inside the bucket. Documents live under notes/, bookkeeping
# under _meta/. Change only if you are sharing one bucket across apps.
# R2_PREFIX=notes
# R2_META_PREFIX=_meta

# Bucket location hint (e.g. "eu"). Leave empty unless Cloudflare told you otherwise.
# R2_JURISDICTION=

# POST a JSON payload here and the app will notify you on unhandled errors.
# ERROR_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Local storage locations. The Electron desktop sets these itself
# (%APPDATA%\MarkForge); leave empty for plain `pnpm dev` / `next start`.
# NOTES_DIR=./notes
# META_DIR=.

# A second bucket used by tests/r2-write.test.ts for live round-trip checks.
# Safe to leave empty if you do not run the storage test suite.
# R2_TEST_BUCKET=
